242
00:14:57,220 --> 00:15:00,680
How you ruled as an evil
king, you may have forgotten.

243
00:15:00,960 --> 00:15:04,640
But you're the one responsible
for the destruction of Egypt.

244
00:15:09,080 --> 00:15:11,860
What's wrong? You okay? I'm fine.

245
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:16,657
It seems this power-hungry king drew his
evil strength from a mysterious stone.

246
00:15:16,740 --> 00:15:19,799
And this stone drew its
strength from another world.

247
00:15:20,240 --> 00:15:23,300
It's that rock they wear
on their neck, isn't it?

248
00:15:23,800 --> 00:15:24,840
I'm not sure.

249
00:15:25,280 --> 00:15:27,339
That's all I was able to translate.

250
00:15:28,440 --> 00:15:29,617
Chill out, man.

251
00:15:29,700 --> 00:15:30,935
You'll blow a gasket.

252
00:15:31,180 --> 00:15:32,945
You guys don't get it, do you?

253
00:15:33,040 --> 00:15:35,037
Those Atlantis freaks are trying to cover

254
00:15:35,120 --> 00:15:38,560
something up about this ancient
mega monster. Of course.

255
00:15:38,800 --> 00:15:40,937
There was probably something
written in those ruins

256
00:15:41,020 --> 00:15:44,037
about how to destroy that
thing before it destroys us.

257
00:15:44,120 --> 00:15:44,960
I get it.

258
00:15:45,220 --> 00:15:48,217
Hey, Joey, I guess you had
your good idea for the year.

259
00:15:48,300 --> 00:15:50,300
The ruins may have been destroyed,

260
00:15:50,440 --> 00:15:52,817
but there are copies of the
inscriptions at a museum.

261
00:15:52,900 --> 00:15:57,020
It's in Florida, where I was doing
my underwater research. Perfect!

262
00:15:57,460 --> 00:16:01,300
So all we have to do is go there
and translate the rest. Mm-hmm.

263
00:16:01,900 --> 00:16:03,620
Hey, what are we waiting for?

264
00:16:03,860 --> 00:16:06,137
Let's head to the Sunshine
State and find out the

265
00:16:06,220 --> 00:16:08,677
secret to defeating these
guys and saving Yugi,

266
00:16:08,760 --> 00:16:09,590
right?

267
00:16:09,673 --> 00:16:11,320
I'm right behind you, man.

268
00:16:11,840 --> 00:16:13,252
Goodbye to Death Valley.

269
00:16:13,380 --> 00:16:15,960
Hello to fun in the sun. That's great.

270
00:16:16,180 --> 00:16:18,717
Just one question, how are
we supposed to get there?

271
00:16:18,800 --> 00:16:19,630
We're doomed.

272
00:16:22,020 --> 00:16:26,717
Ever since these monster sightings began,
Kyber Corp's stock's been plummeting, sir.

273
00:16:26,800 --> 00:16:30,637
And almost half of our company's
been bought by some unknown investor.

274
00:16:30,720 --> 00:16:32,720
I think I know who it is.

275
00:16:32,860 --> 00:16:37,095
But just to be sure, I need you to
trace those transactions immediately.

276
00:16:37,420 --> 00:16:41,200
And when you do, I'm sure they'll
point straight to Pegasus.

277
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:46,380
He's been after my company for years,
and I'd sooner see it destroyed.

278
00:16:48,940 --> 00:16:52,980
Uh, Seto, I'm not so sure
it's Pegasus who's doing this.

279
00:16:53,420 --> 00:16:55,660
I mean, couldn't it be Alistair?

280
00:16:55,820 --> 00:16:57,140
He was pretty upset.

281
00:16:58,720 --> 00:17:00,320
Kaiba, see this?

282
00:17:01,140 --> 00:17:05,640
It used to be my brother's,
but I'll never see him again.

283
00:17:06,560 --> 00:17:08,817
Because your father took him away from me.

284
00:17:08,900 --> 00:17:12,100
He blames Kaiba Corp for
what happened to his brother.

285
00:17:12,420 --> 00:17:16,340
And if I were Alistar, I'd
probably blame this company, too.

286
00:17:17,560 --> 00:17:21,997
Besides, Yugi said Pegasus had his soul
captured, so he can't be behind this Seto.

287
00:17:22,080 --> 00:17:25,620
Mokuba, I don't know about
all that Pegasus nonsense,

288
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:28,860
but you do bring up a
good point about Alistar.

289
00:17:30,780 --> 00:17:32,800
So you agree? Maybe.

290
00:17:34,980 --> 00:17:35,940
What is it?

291
00:17:36,580 --> 00:17:37,540
There's a Mr.

292
00:17:37,740 --> 00:17:39,681
Wheeler on the line for you, sir.

293
00:17:40,380 --> 00:17:41,380
It's Joey!

294
00:17:42,140 --> 00:17:44,080
Oh, great. Put him through.

295
00:17:44,600 --> 00:17:45,430
Yes, sir.

296
00:17:47,200 --> 00:17:50,200
He really took your call? What? He did?

297
00:17:50,860 --> 00:17:51,690
Diva!

298
00:17:51,840 --> 00:17:53,075
Is that you in there?

299
00:17:53,400 --> 00:17:57,080
It works better when you
step back from the webcam.

300
00:17:57,600 --> 00:17:58,430
Eh?

301
00:18:00,040 --> 00:18:01,100
Hey, you're right.

302
00:18:01,360 --> 00:18:02,720
Make it fast, Wheeler.

303
00:18:02,920 --> 00:18:05,508
We found some clues
about those biker punks.

304
00:18:05,820 --> 00:18:07,140
What kind of clues?

305
00:18:07,560 --> 00:18:10,031
I'm not giving them up that easily, Kaiba.

306
00:18:10,360 --> 00:18:13,577
But if you give us a lift to
Florida, I'll fill you in on the way.

307
00:18:13,660 --> 00:18:14,954
So what's it gonna be?

308
00:18:15,260 --> 00:18:16,600
Time is running out.

309
00:18:16,860 --> 00:18:19,507
Those creeps defeated
Yugi and Pook his soul.

310
00:18:22,120 --> 00:18:24,800
Way to keep a secret, lame brain.

311
00:18:25,440 --> 00:18:26,270
Yugi's soul?

312
00:18:26,500 --> 00:18:27,382
What's he mean?

313
00:18:29,760 --> 00:18:31,917
Please disregard my last statement, folks.

314
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:33,140
Whatever.

315
00:18:33,460 --> 00:18:36,257
Kaiba doesn't believe in
all that magic stuff anyway.

316
00:18:36,340 --> 00:18:40,140
Yeah, it's all some kind
of Hocus Pocus mind trick.

317
00:18:40,780 --> 00:18:42,740
Hey, that sounds just like it.

318
00:18:46,960 --> 00:18:48,320
Yugi lost!

319
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:54,180
Yugi gave his Duel Monsters
Championship crown to some nobody?

320
00:18:54,840 --> 00:18:57,560
No one deserves that title but me!

321
00:18:59,160 --> 00:19:00,037
Hold on.

322
00:19:00,120 --> 00:19:02,580
I don't want to hear another word.

323
00:19:02,880 --> 00:19:05,140
You're a disgrace to the game, Yugi.

324
00:19:09,400 --> 00:19:10,660
Seto, you okay?

325
00:19:12,620 --> 00:19:13,720
I'm fine.

326
00:19:14,080 --> 00:19:18,320
Now I have one more incentive to
hunt down and destroy those thugs.

327
00:19:19,020 --> 00:19:20,020
Now what?

328
00:19:20,920 --> 00:19:22,780
Oh, Ride, that stinks.

329
00:19:23,440 --> 00:19:24,280
That jerk!

330
00:19:24,600 --> 00:19:26,857
How are we supposed to
get down to Florida now?

331
00:19:26,940 --> 00:19:30,764
Well, I say the professor stays
here, and we hop the next flight.

332
00:19:31,080 --> 00:19:32,260
He's right, Gramps.

333
00:19:32,480 --> 00:19:35,917
Running around the country is not
the best thing for you right now.

334
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:39,706
Duke, why don't you stay here
and keep an eye on the professor?

335
00:19:40,740 --> 00:19:41,570
Sure.

336
00:19:41,653 --> 00:19:44,298
So I guess a private jet is
out of the question, huh?

337
00:19:45,520 --> 00:19:48,577
I'll book our flights, and we'll
take a train to the airport.

338
00:19:48,660 --> 00:19:51,760
I just hope we can save
Yugi before it's too late.
